\begin{abstract}
In this paper, we formulate a framework for the universal quantum isometry group acting on spectral triples within Alain Connes' noncommutative geometry. By defining a suitable category of isometric coactions of compact quantum groups on a spectral triple $(\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{H}, D)$ that preserve the Dirac operator $D$, we prove the existence and uniqueness of a universal object acting as the maximal quantum symmetry group of the underlying noncommutative Riemannian manifold. As a explicit application, we apply this construction to the geometry of the quantum double torus, extending the topological and algebraic structures investigated by Hajac~\cite{hajac}. We explicitly compute the generator relations of the corresponding quantum isometry group, demonstrating how the noncommutativity of the quantum double torus deforms classical isometric symmetries into genuine compact quantum groups. Our results provide new insights into the interplay between spectral geometry and non-abelian quantum symmetries.
\end{abstract}
